claimed: acme-eab -- External Account Binding (RFC 8555 §7.3.4), the first of the three remaining ACME items the operator asked for all of. Some CAs (ZeroSSL, Google Trust Services, most commercial ones) will not open an account without proof you already have one with them: the newAccount request carries an `externalAccountBinding` -- an inner JWS over the account's OWN public JWK, signed HS256 with a key id and MAC key the CA gave you out of band, whose protected header names that kid and the newAccount URL. Acme.Config gains `eab: Option[(String, String)]` (kid, base64url MAC key); the signing is ~30 lines over the Crypto seam's hmacSha256. Tested for real: Pebble with externalAccountBindingRequired mounted as its config refuses an account without the binding and issues with it. Touches Acme.scala, Serve.scala (OKAY_ACME_EAB=kid:key), specs/acme.md, docs.
